    55	## 1. Exact LP barrier and upper-bound certificate (C2–C3)
    56	
    57	Let P be a rank-K projector on n qubits. Use the standard Shor–Laflamme enumerators
    58	
    59	`A_j = sum_{wt(E)=j} |Tr(PE)|^2`,
    60	
    61	`B_j = sum_{wt(E)=j} Tr(PEPE)`
    62	
    63	for Hermitian Pauli strings E. Put `a_j=A_j/K^2`, `b_j=B_j/K`. The established MacWilliams identity and shadow inequalities [P3, Eqs. (5)–(11)] give
    64	
    65	`b_j = (K/2^n) sum_i K_j(i;n) a_i`,
    66	
    67	`s_j = (1/2^n) sum_i (-1)^i K_j(i;n) a_i >= 0`,
    68	
    69	where `K_j(i;n)` is the coefficient of `x^(n-j)y^j` in `(x+3y)^(n-i)(x-y)^i`.
    70	
    71	Necessary conditions at distance at least d are:
    72	
    73	- `a_0=1`, all `a_j>=0`;
    74	- `b_j=a_j` for `0<=j<d`;
    75	- `b_j>=a_j` for all remaining j;
    76	- every `s_j>=0`.
    77	
    78	These conditions permit degenerate codes. We do not add purity, integrality, CWS, or stabilizer restrictions to the general-code LP.
    79	
    80	### C2: a rational feasible point at K=3
    81	
    82	For `n=7, K=3, d=3`, take
    83	
    84	```text
    85	a = (1, 0, 0, 0, 7, 14, 56/3, 2)
    86	b = (1, 0, 0, 28, 63, 126, 112, 54)
    87	s = (1/12, 0, 7/4, 28/3, 49/4, 56, 343/12, 20).
    88	```
    89	
    90	Every listed condition follows by direct rational substitution. `results/lp-feasible-7-3-3.json` stores a. The independent verifier obtains the transforms by repeated polynomial multiplication, not by importing the generator's binomial Krawtchouk formula.
    91	
    92	This settles the proposed **LP-only** route negatively: no correct infeasibility certificate for these exact constraints exists at this target. It does **not** settle the complete SDP hierarchy, stronger relaxations, or existence of a physical projector realizing this enumerator.
    93	
    94	### C3: explicit contradiction at K=4
    95	
    96	For n=7 define the integer linear forms
    97	
    98	`F_j = 4 sum_i K_j(i;7) a_i - 128 a_j`,
    99	
   100	`T_j = sum_i (-1)^i K_j(i;7) a_i`.
   101	
   102	A distance-three code with K=4 requires `F_0=F_1=F_2=0` and `T_0,T_1>=0`. Coefficient-by-coefficient polynomial expansion gives the **identical zero linear form**
   103	
   104	```text
   105	0 = a_0 + 4 a_1 + a_2 + 2 a_3
   106	    + (T_0 + T_1)/16
   107	    - 5 F_0/128 - F_1/64 - F_2/128.
   108	```
   109	
   110	Substitution of the necessary constraints makes the right-hand side at least 1, a contradiction. All nonnegative multipliers and equality multipliers are in `results/lp-infeasible-7-4-3.json`. The verifier checks every coefficient is exactly zero and the normalized contradiction constant is exactly one.
   111	
   112	If a code of dimension greater than four existed, any four-dimensional subspace would inherit every Knill–Laflamme error-detection identity. Thus C3 excludes all `K>=4`, not only exactly K=4. Together with C1 it certifies the known interval `2 <= K_max(7,3) <= 3`.
