README.md:26:It needs Python, NetworkX and NumPy, but no internet, LP/SDP solver, GPU, or model call. It checks rational identities, two independent distance representations for each explicit code, all 1,044 seven-vertex graph representatives, all 32 eleven-vertex circulant frames, and four negative controls across the two programs. The complete analytic arguments, trust boundaries, observed output and review dispositions are in [RESULTS.md](RESULTS.md). The analytic dimension lemma is not machine-formalized by the command.
